* ''A lock always drops its signer'' (controller, 2026-11-07). Security outranks durability: a seal or open ask ends on its answer, the island's exit, or a named `LIVENESS` silence bound that refuses; the signer drops in every case, and a save left unsealed waits in memory by name, never rests clear.

